       PROCESS APOST.
       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.

       PROGRAM-ID.       TWO2EDW2.
       INSTALLATION.
       AUTHOR.           D. BARAONA.
       DATE-WRITTEN.     09/2018.

      *************************************************************
      *  SEND WORK ORDERS BY PART NUMBER TO EDW THROUGH FTP.
      *      -SELECT WORK ORDERS FROM WO PARTS FILE MCFLMM1201
      *        SENDING THE WHOLE MCFLMM1201 FILE
      *      -SELECT PART INFORMATION FROM CODE DESCRIPTION FILE MCFLCS1401
      *        SENDING THE WHOLE MCFLCS1401 FILE
      *      -THESE FILES SHARE THE PART NUMBER FIELD (PRTNO)
      *      -ADD THE PLANT CODE (I.E. N501) TO EACH OUTPUT RECORD
      *           AS THE FIRST 4 DIGITS.
      *
      *      -WRITES TO FILES MCFP120EDW AND MCFP140EDW FOR EDW.
      *
      *  CPPI 2016-27276561  MMIS TO EDW INTERFACE
      **************************************************************

       ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
       CONFIGURATION SECTION.

       SOURCE-COMPUTER.  IBM-AS-400.
       OBJECT-COMPUTER.  IBM-AS-400.

       SPECIAL-NAMES.    REQUESTOR IS WORK-STATION
                         SYSTEM-CONSOLE IS CONSOLE
                         SYSTEM-SHUTDOWN IS SHUTDOWN-SWITCH
                           ON STATUS IS SYSTEM-SHUTDOWN-REQUESTED.

       INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
       FILE-CONTROL.

      *MCFLMM1201 - Workorder Part by WO          INPUT
            SELECT MCFLMM1201-FILE
                   ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFLMM1201
                   ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
                   ACCESS IS DYNAMIC
                   RECORD KEY IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
                   WITH DUPLICATES
                   FILE STATUS IS MCFLMM1201-SK.

      *MCFLCS1401 - Code Description              INPUT
            SELECT MCFLCS1401-FILE
                   ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFLCS1401
                   ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
                   ACCESS IS DYNAMIC
                   RECORD KEY IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
                   WITH DUPLICATES
                   FILE STATUS IS MCFLCS1401-SK.

      *MCFP120EDW - FOR EDW- WO-PARTS    Send to EDW       OUTPUT
            SELECT MCFP120EDW-FILE
                   ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFP120EDW
                   ORGANIZATION IS SEQUENTIAL
                   ACCESS IS SEQUENTIAL
                   FILE STATUS IS MCFP120EDW-SK.

      *MCFP140EDW - FOR EDW -Code Description DDESC  Send to EDW  OUTPUT
            SELECT MCFP140EDW-FILE
                   ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFP140EDW
                   ORGANIZATION IS SEQUENTIAL
                   ACCESS IS SEQUENTIAL
                   FILE STATUS IS MCFP140EDW-SK.

      *MCFLCS0501 - Read for the PLANT CODE by key ID      INPUT
            SELECT MCFLCS0501-FILE
                   ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFLCS0501
                   ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
                   ACCESS IS DYNAMIC
                   RECORD KEY IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
                   FILE STATUS IS MCFLCS0501-SK.

       DATA DIVISION.
       FILE SECTION.
       FD  MCFLMM1201-FILE.
       01  MCFLMM1201-REC.
           COPY DDS-ALL-FORMATS OF MCFLMM1201.

       FD  MCFLCS1401-FILE.
       01  MCFLCS1401-REC.
           COPY DDS-ALL-FORMATS OF MCFLCS1401.

       FD  MCFP120EDW-FILE.
       01  MCFP120EDW-REC.
           COPY DDS-ALL-FORMATS OF MCFP120EDW.

       FD  MCFP140EDW-FILE.
       01  MCFP140EDW-REC.
           COPY DDS-ALL-FORMATS OF MCFP140EDW.

       FD  MCFLCS0501-FILE.
       01  MCFLCS0501-REC.
           COPY DDS-MCRPCS0500  OF MCFLCS0501.
      *    COPY MPLTSAP IN COPYLIB. Used what I needed below.
      *------- KEY = 'SAP'.
           06  MPLTINFO-SAP REDEFINES PLTINFODTA.
               10  MPLTINFO-SAP-SEND-SWK           PIC X(1).
               10  MPLTINFO-SAP-PRINT-SWK          PIC X(1).
               10  MPLTINFO-SAP-SET-AUTH-FLAG      PIC X(1).
               10  MPLTINFO-SAP-HIDE-Q1-SW         PIC X(1).
               10  MPLT-NUMBER                     PIC X(4).
               10  FILLER                          PIC X(52).


       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
       01  MCFLMM1201-SK     PIC  X(02) VALUE SPACES.
       01  MCFLCS1401-SK     PIC  X(02) VALUE SPACES.
       01  MCFP120EDW-SK     PIC  X(02) VALUE SPACES.
       01  MCFP140EDW-SK     PIC  X(02) VALUE SPACES.
       01  MCFLCS0501-SK     PIC  X(02) VALUE SPACES.
       01  RET-CODE          PIC X(10).

       01  HOLD-PLANT            PIC X(4) VALUE SPACES.

       01  HOLD-RECORD1.
           05  HOLD-PLANT1       PIC X(4) VALUE SPACES.
           05  HOLD-REC120EDW    PIC X(750) VALUE SPACES.
       01  HOLD-RECORD2.
           05  HOLD-PLANT2       PIC X(4) VALUE SPACES.
           05  HOLD-REC140EDW    PIC X(90) VALUE SPACES.


       LINKAGE SECTION.

      *********************
       PROCEDURE DIVISION.

       000-MAIN.
           PERFORM 1000-OPEN-FILES.
           IF RET-CODE NOT = SPACES
               GO TO EOJ.

      * GET PLANT LOCATION
           MOVE 'XXXX' TO MPLT-NUMBER.
           MOVE 'SAP' TO PLTINFOKEY OF MCRPCS0500
           READ MCFLCS0501-FILE
                INVALID KEY DISPLAY '******************************'
                            DISPLAY '***  NO PLANT VALUE FOUND  ***'
                            DISPLAY '*** Error in PGM=MMISEDWXFR **'
                            DISPLAY '******************************'
                            GO TO EOJ
           END-READ.
           MOVE MPLT-NUMBER TO HOLD-PLANT.

      *Position to beginning of MCFLMM1201 Workorder Parts file
           MOVE SPACES TO WONUM OF MCRPMM1200.
           START MCFLMM1201-FILE
                KEY IS NOT LESS THAN EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
                INVALID KEY CONTINUE.

           READ MCFLMM1201-FILE NEXT RECORD
                AT END CONTINUE.
           PERFORM 300-WRITE-120EDW-REC
               UNTIL MCFLMM1201-SK NOT = '00'.

      *Position to beginning of MCFLCS1401 Corp Code description file
           MOVE SPACES TO CORPCDE OF MCRPCS1400.
           START MCFLCS1401-FILE
                KEY IS NOT LESS THAN EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
                INVALID KEY CONTINUE.

           READ MCFLCS1401-FILE NEXT RECORD
               AT END CONTINUE.
           PERFORM 400-WRITE-140EDW-REC
             UNTIL MCFLCS1401-SK IS NOT = '00'.

       EOJ.
           CLOSE MCFLMM1201-FILE
                 MCFLCS1401-FILE
                 MCFP120EDW-FILE
                 MCFP140EDW-FILE
                 MCFLCS0501-FILE.
           STOP RUN.
           EXIT PROGRAM.

       300-WRITE-120EDW-REC.
           INITIALIZE HOLD-REC120EDW.
           MOVE HOLD-PLANT TO HOLD-PLANT1.
           MOVE MCFLMM1201-REC TO HOLD-REC120EDW.
           WRITE MCFP120EDW-REC FROM HOLD-RECORD1.
           IF MCFP120EDW-SK NOT = '00'
                MOVE 'BAD120EDW' TO RET-CODE
                DISPLAY '*************************************'
                DISPLAY 'BAD WRITE ON MCFP120EDW-FILE'
                DISPLAY 'IN PGM=TWO2EDW2'
                DISPLAY 'MCFP120EDW-SK = ' MCFP120EDW-SK
                DISPLAY '*************************************'.
           READ MCFLMM1201-FILE NEXT RECORD
                AT END CONTINUE.

       400-WRITE-140EDW-REC.
           INITIALIZE HOLD-REC140EDW.
           MOVE HOLD-PLANT TO HOLD-PLANT2.
           MOVE MCFLCS1401-REC TO HOLD-REC140EDW.
           WRITE MCFP140EDW-REC FROM HOLD-RECORD2.
           IF MCFP140EDW-SK NOT = '00'
                MOVE 'BAD140EDW' TO RET-CODE
                DISPLAY '*************************************'
                DISPLAY 'BAD WRITE ON MCFP140EDW-FILE'
                DISPLAY 'IN PGM=TWO2EDW2'
                DISPLAY 'MCFP140EDW-SK = ' MCFP140EDW-SK
                DISPLAY '*************************************'.
           READ MCFLCS1401-FILE NEXT RECORD
               AT END CONTINUE.

       1000-OPEN-FILES.
           MOVE SPACES TO RET-CODE.

           OPEN INPUT MCFLMM1201-FILE.
           IF MCFLMM1201-SK NOT = '00'
               DISPLAY '***************************************'
               DISPLAY 'BAD OPEN ON MCFLMM1201-FILE'
               DISPLAY 'IN PGM=MMISEDWXFR'
               DISPLAY 'MCFLMM1201-SK = ' MCFLMM1201-SK
               DISPLAY 'PROGRAM ABENDING'
               DISPLAY 'CONTACT AKRON - CHECK JOB LOG'
               DISPLAY '***************************************'
               MOVE 'BADOPEN' TO RET-CODE.

           OPEN INPUT MCFLCS1401-FILE.
           IF MCFLCS1401-SK NOT = '00'
               DISPLAY '***************************************'
               DISPLAY 'BAD OPEN ON MCFLCS1401-FILE'
               DISPLAY 'IN PGM=MMISEDWXFR'
               DISPLAY 'MCFLCS1401-SK = ' MCFLCS1401-SK
               DISPLAY 'CONTACT AKRON - CHECK JOB LOG'
               DISPLAY '***************************************'
               MOVE 'BADOPEN' TO RET-CODE.

           OPEN OUTPUT MCFP120EDW-FILE.
           IF MCFP120EDW-SK NOT = '00'
               DISPLAY '***************************************'
               DISPLAY 'BAD OPEN ON MCFP120EDW-FILE'
               DISPLAY 'IN PGM=TWO2EDW2'
               DISPLAY 'MCFP120EDW-SK = ' MCFP120EDW-SK
               DISPLAY 'CONTACT AKRON - CHECK JOB LOG'
               DISPLAY '***************************************'
               MOVE 'BADOPEN' TO RET-CODE.

           OPEN OUTPUT MCFP140EDW-FILE.
           IF MCFP140EDW-SK NOT = '00'
               DISPLAY '***************************************'
               DISPLAY 'BAD OPEN ON MCFP140EDW-FILE'
               DISPLAY 'IN PGM=TWO2EDW2'
               DISPLAY 'MCFP140EDW-SK = ' MCFP140EDW-SK
               DISPLAY 'CONTACT AKRON - CHECK JOB LOG'
               DISPLAY '***************************************'
               MOVE 'BADOPEN' TO RET-CODE.

           OPEN INPUT MCFLCS0501-FILE.
           IF MCFLCS0501-SK NOT = '00'
               DISPLAY '***************************************'
               DISPLAY 'BAD OPEN ON MCFLCS0501-FILE'
               DISPLAY 'IN PGM=MMISEDWXFR'
               DISPLAY 'MCFLCS0501-SK = ' MCFLCS0501-SK
               DISPLAY 'CONTACT AKRON - CHECK JOB LOG'
               DISPLAY '***************************************'
               MOVE 'BADOPEN' TO RET-CODE.
